                    "a": "(c) Ionocytes — Fresh water animals have specialized cells called ionocytes in their gills and skin which actively extract Na+, Cl- and Ca++ from the external medium and excrete H+ or HCO3- for acid base balance in the body fluids.",
                    "q": "(iii) Fresh water organisms also have specialized cells located in their gills and in skin which actively extract Na+, Cl- and Ca+ from external medium and excrete (H+) or basic (HCO3-) for acid base balance in the body fluids are called\n(a) Granulocyte\n(b) Lymphocyte\n(c) Ionocytes\n(d) podocyte"
