                    "q": "(viii) The catalyst commonly used in the conversion of sulfur dioxide to sulfur trioxide during the preparation of sulphuric acid is:\n(a) Vanadium pentoxide (V2O5) (b) Copper (Cu) (c) Iron (Fe) (d) Nickel (Ni)"
