                    "a": "Phenol (pKa ≈ 10) is a much stronger acid than ethanol (pKa ≈ 16) because the phenoxide ion is stabilized by resonance (charge delocalized over the ring), while the ethoxide ion has a localized charge on oxygen. Phenol is soluble in water (about 8 g/100 mL) but less soluble than ethanol, which is completely miscible with water, because the large benzene ring is non-polar.",
