                    "a": "Spectroscopy is the study of the interaction of electromagnetic radiation of light with matter. It is a powerful analytical technique for the determination of the structure of molecules. It is favoured over conventional chemical tests because: it is easier and takes very little time to analyze a sample; it requires a very small amount of substance; and it provides more reliable information about the chemical molecule.",
                    "q": "What is spectroscopy? Why is it favoured over conventional methods?"
