                    "a": "A NAND gate is an AND gate followed by a NOT gate: X = (A·B)′. Its output is 0 only when all inputs are 1. A NOR gate is an OR gate followed by a NOT gate: X = (A + B)′. Its output is 1 only when all inputs are 0.",
